SECTION 2: TRANSFER MATRIX = COMPRESSED PROJECTION PRODUCT
============================================================

The transfer matrix M(x) compresses the n-1-fold product
into a 3-state Markov chain. This works because:
  1. The Z_j variables have TRIDIAGONAL covariance
     (E[Z_j Z_k] = 0 for |j-k| >= 2)
  2. The non-adjacent FACTORIZATION: E[prod Z_j] factorizes
     over connected components of the position set
  3. Each component's weight depends only on its SIZE,
     not on its POSITION (translation invariance of pair stats)

These three properties follow from the WEIGHT FORMULA:
  E[prod Z_j for S] = 2^c / (n)_L
which itself follows from the MONOTONE WALK argument.

